# Build artifacts  -  target directories at any depth.
target/
**/target/
*/target/
**/target-*/
conform/fuzz/target/
/book/

# Cargo lock backup.
Cargo.lock.old

# Temporary cargo target directories (e.g. CI / tooling).
**/.cargo-target-*
**/.cargo-target/
/tmp/cargo-target-*

# Mutation testing.
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/
*.rlib

# proptest regression corpus  -  regenerated deterministically from seeds.
# See scripts/fetch-regressions.sh.
conform/regressions/

# Profiling / flamegraph artifacts.
*.profdata
*.profraw
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg

# Editor / IDE scratch.
.vscode/
.idea/
.cursor/
**/.cursor/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Python/test cache artifacts.
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/

# Generated split scratch emitted by local organization experiments.
**/__law7_split/

# Merge / rebase leftovers.
*.orig
*.rej

# macOS.
.DS_Store

# Local operator/agent-only material: never export to the public Vyre repo.
/.internals/
/jules_tickets/
/jules-tickets/
/.jules/
/jules/

# Local rule drops used during private sweeps; shipped rule fixtures live in crate-owned paths.
/rules/
/.rules/

# Operational planning, status, audit, and agent-handoff files are private
# operator state, not public prod repo source. The root-only patterns below came
# first; the `**/` patterns extend the same policy to every depth, because these
# files kept getting staged out of subdirectories (docs/archive/, docs/legacy/,
# audits/, docs/optimization/, per-crate .audits/) and would otherwise land in
# public history. Public-facing docs use descriptive names and live outside these
# patterns; if a doc is meant for users, it must not be named *PLAN*/*STATUS*/
# *AUDIT*/AGENT_*.
/STATUS.md
/ROADMAP.md
/UPGRADE_PLAN.md
/*STATUS*.md
/*ROADMAP*.md
/*PLAN*.md
**/*PLAN*.md
**/*STATUS*.md
**/*ROADMAP*.md
**/*AUDIT*.md
**/*BACKLOG*.md
**/AGENT_*.md
**/GEMINI_HANDOFF_*.md
**/.audits/

# Local generated adversarial registry closure scratch. Real adversarial tests
# should be committed under crate-owned test names with specific assertions.
**/tests/adversarial_registry_closure.rs

# Single private execution queue (STANDARD.md)
/BACKLOG.md
